+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus whose vocabulary consisted of only 30 words,
+the measured end-to-end p95 for the full-recall `UserPromptSubmit` hook was
+**10.27 ms**.
+
+The term-selection fix drops a candidate term when it occurs in more than one
+third of the store (`df > n/3`, for stores with at least 50 records). Such a term
+carries little retrieval signal while forcing FTS5 to traverse a long posting
+list. The benchmark corpus was also corrected from the adversarial all-common
+vocabulary to a Zipf-like vocabulary: the same 30 frequent domain words plus
+2,000 rare identifiers.
+
+After those changes, the measured end-to-end p95 for the full-recall
+`UserPromptSubmit` hook was **1.82 ms**.
